l steel alloyed with shavings from the Labyrinth. <br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T17:11:39-08:00","id":1057346,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Dammit! <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar408_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"408\" data-vbnamecard=\"408\">nothing</a> is correct. I was thinking of darksteel vs Stygian steel. Carry on.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T07:41:28-08:00","id":1057592,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Nothing. Is there a mechanical difference besides Stygian steel causing aggravated damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T08:30:39-08:00","id":1060103,"title":"","content":"Offhand I can't think of one. I think when it is surgically installed (mentioned in Doomslayers) it reduces Permanent Corpus for the duration, but that might just be because of the surgery itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T08:33:27-08:00","id":1060104,"title":"","content":"I believe Stygian Steel is also stronger then Soulsteel. I consider it Soulsteel + what with it resonating with Oblivion cast offs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T08:38:05-08:00","id":1060108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1057202-is-there-a-difference-between-stygian-steel-and-soulsteel?p=1060104#post1060104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe Stygian Steel is also stronger then Soulsteel. I consider it Soulsteel + what with it resonating with Oblivion cast offs.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely stated to be stronger, I just don't know if that comes up mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T11:28:41-07:00","id":1062882,"title":"","content":"Having scoured the books before for this question, I can tell you there isn't a whole lot printed about it. So, if you want it to have more benefits, go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T05:35:55-07:00","id":1128016,"title":"","content":"Isn't Stygian steel aggravated since it carries the taint of oblivion, whereas soulsteel is just lethal?<br /> <br /> Also Stygian steel is more durable for sure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T16:29:54-07:00","id":1131005,"title":"","content":"From the Artificers Guildbook:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Stygian Steel (and the cheap stuff):</b><br /> There are a variety of materials that can be worked with<br /> soulfire. The two most common are pure plasm, sometimes<br /> called soul-steel, and Stygian steel. The former is the pure<br /> soul essence of human beings, heated and hammered. Oboli<br /> are made from soul-steel, as are most of the weapons of the<br /> Legions and many of the buildings and bridges of the City<br /> of Chains. Most Artificers can only forge soul-steel, but this<br /> material serves their purposes.<br /> Stygian Steel is something else again. An alloy of souls,<br /> the \u201cdeath ore\u201d that makes up the islands in the Tempest,<br /> and the raw stuff of Oblivion scraped from the walls of the<br /> Labyrinth, Stygian steel cuts through soul-steel with hardly<br /> a hitch, and as such Stygian steel weapons are coveted by<br /> Deathlords and the other mighty of Stygia. It is rare that an<br /> Artificer below Forgemaster rank is capable of working with<br /> Stygian steel, and anyone without the requisite skill (at least<br /> four points in Soulforging) who attempts to work with the raw<br /> Oblivion necessary will inevitably destroy all of the materials<br /> with which he's working.<br /> Between these two extremes lies an alloy of \u201cdeath ore\u201d<br /> and souls that is marginally tougher and stronger than soulsteel.<br /> Sometimes called Necropolis steel, it takes longer to<br /> work than plain soul-steel. Many soulforgers don't consider<br /> the extra effort worth it. </div> </div> </div>Still doesn't say much about the mechanical properties, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}